              "title": "Folge 13",
              "season": 1,
              "episode": 13,
              "show": {
                "id": 51198,
                "thetvdb_id": 479625,
                "title": "Eden - Du bezahlst für jede Lüge",
                "in_account": false,
                "slug": "eden-du-bezahlst-fur-jede-luge",
                "creation": "2026",
                "status": "Continuing",
                "description": "The concept of the “most honest of all dating shows” according to Joyn and ProSieben: 13 singles are looking for their perfect match. Only those who end up as a couple have the chance to win up to 100,000 euros. The catch: The candidates are regularly asked to take a lie detector to test their authenticity. For every untruth or lie, 1,000 euros will be deducted from the group's jackpot. According to the announcement, the questions are “merciless”. The participants have to answer questions like: “Are your feelings real?” and “Did you secretly kiss someone else yesterday?” or “Is getting to know each other just a game for you?”\r\nThe moral dilemma for the candidates: Anyone who lies to save the fresh romance reduces the budget of the entire group. On the other hand, if you stick to the painful truth, you save the prize money, but you risk the immediate end of the date. In this way, “Eden” should become the “ultimate endurance test” for everyone getting to know each other. (Text: GR)"
              },
